<%# THE GOALS STRIP. Rendered by the ALL tab; its two readers are `Dashboard::OverviewPresenter`'s
    since task 5 moved them off the deleted `Dashboard::SavingsPresenter`.

    SAVINGS ARE CATEGORIES NOW (two-ledger spec §3, Task 7) — `_pools_strip` renamed with the
    thing it draws. Each card links to the category's own page, which is where a goal's figure,
    its target and its history all live since the Pools screens were deleted. The classifier is
    `Category#saving_toward_a_target?` (see the presenter): a funding start and a target to reach.

    ** THE FIGURE IS A CLAIM AND THE STRIP NAMES NO MOMENT (computed-claims §§2-3). ** It used to be
    a HOLDING bounded at `period_range.end` — money that had been moved in by that date, less what
    was spent — and there is no such balance any more. What a category has is what its rules claim,
    computed from the calendar and the spending; the presenter's `#as_of` explains what bounding a
    walk at a past month can and cannot mean, and the short of it is that the bound is
    PERIOD-grained rather than day-grained. So nothing here says "as of", prints a date, or promises
    a month's closing figure: the cards carry a name, a claim, a target and a bar, all of which are
    true whichever month is selected.

    ** THE NEGATIVE ARM IS GONE, NOT GATED. ** §3 clamps every claim at zero — a rate rule's at
    `max(0, …)`, an accruing rule's into `0..target` — so no row here can carry a negative figure,
    and the card's red "negative" badge and the total's `text-terracotta` were branches nothing
    could reach. `home/_hero.html.erb`'s rule: an unreachable branch on a money screen is a sentence
    waiting to be believed. What the old branch was really about — spending past what a fund had —
    is `ClaimCalculator#over?`, which Home's own rows and trouble strip report; a strip whose whole
    subject is progress toward a target is not the place to re-derive it. %>
<% goals = @presenter.savings_summary %>
<% if goals.any? %>
  <div class="mb-8" data-savings-strip>
    <div class="mb-4">
      <h3 class="text-lg font-medium text-gray-900">Savings Goals</h3>
      <p class="text-sm text-gray-500">
        Claimed: <span class="font-semibold text-brand-dark"><%= number_to_currency(@presenter.total_savings_balance) %></span>
      </p>
    </div>
    <div class="grid grid-cols-1 sm:grid-cols-2 lg:grid-cols-3 gap-4">
      <% goals.each do |goal| %>
        <% progress = goal[:progress_percentage] %>

        <%# Status based purely on how much of the target the rules claim. See the header for why
            there is no negative arm: a claim cannot be negative. %>
        <% if progress < 10 && goal[:target_amount].positive? %>
          <% card_class = "border-2 border-status-warning/40 bg-status-warning-light" %>
          <% bar_class = "bg-status-warning" %>
          <% badge_class = "text-status-warning bg-status-warning/20" %>
          <% badge_text = "low" %>
        <% elsif progress >= 100 %>
          <% card_class = "border border-gray-100 bg-gray-50" %>
          <% bar_class = "bg-brand-dark" %>
          <% badge_class = "text-brand-dark bg-brand/20" %>
          <% badge_text = "funded" %>
        <% elsif progress >= 50 %>
          <% card_class = "border border-gray-100 bg-gray-50" %>
          <% bar_class = "bg-brand-dark" %>
          <% badge_class = "text-brand-dark bg-brand/20" %>
          <% badge_text = "#{progress}%" %>
        <% else %>
          <% card_class = "border border-gray-100 bg-gray-50" %>
          <% bar_class = "bg-brand-dark" %>
          <% badge_class = "text-gray-500 bg-gray-200" %>
          <% badge_text = "#{progress}%" %>
        <% end %>

        <%= link_to category_path(goal[:id]),
            class: "block rounded p-4 hover:opacity-90 transition #{card_class}" do %>
          <div class="flex items-center justify-between mb-2">
            <p class="text-sm font-medium text-gray-900 truncate"><%= goal[:name] %></p>
            <span class="text-xs font-medium px-2 py-0.5 rounded shrink-0 <%= badge_class %>"><%= badge_text %></span>
          </div>
          <div class="w-full bg-gray-200 rounded-full h-3 mb-2">
            <div class="h-3 rounded-full <%= bar_class %>" style="width: <%= progress.clamp(0, 100) %>%"></div>
          </div>
          <%# THE PER-PERIOD "In / Out" ROW IS DELETED (plan 3, task 4). "In" read
              `Pool#contribution_entries` — savings-TYPED entries — so it printed $0.00 on every
              card while the demo's goals were visibly receiving $525 a period: a figure that
              denies money that arrived is worse than no figure. "Out" alone is half a story. The
              figure, the target and the progress bar stay, and all three are now `ClaimLedger`'s —
              `Σ` of the category's rules' claims (computed-claims §3), which is the app's one
              answer to what a category has. %>
          <div class="flex items-center justify-between text-xs text-gray-500">
            <span class="font-medium"><%= number_to_currency(goal[:balance]) %></span>
            <span>of <%= number_to_currency(goal[:target_amount]) %></span>
          </div>
        <% end %>
      <% end %>
    </div>
  </div>
<% end %>
